re is no FDA-approved maximum daily dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"Not FDA-approved/currently marketed","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Not FDA-approved/currently marketed","rationale":"No current FDA/openFDA label was identified, so there is no FDA-approved minimum effective dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"Historical/non-U.S. dosing individualized","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Historical/non-U.S. dosing varied by trial; no current FDA-approved dosing.","rationale":"The cited trials used historical regimens rather than current approved dosing. Martinez-Lage used divided daily dosing; Schmidt reported an average daily dose of 2100 mg in a small add-on trial.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6382068/"]},{"current_value":"Not FDA-cleared; ANSM France authorization 19/04/1984, revoked 21/07/2014","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"Not FDA-cleared/approved; retain the French authorization/revocation dates only with the cited ANSM/public medicines-directory source.","rationale":"The FDA portion is supported by no FDA/openFDA label. The exact French dates are not verifiable from the allowed source domains supplied for this audit.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"GABA analog/prodrug with agonist activity at GABA-A and GABA-B receptors, enhancing inhibitory GABAergic signaling.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"GABA analog/prodrug with GABA-receptor agonist activity, including GABA-A/GABA-B activity reported in pharmacology records, enhancing inhibitory GABAergic signaling.","rationale":"PubMed pharmacology evidence supports specific GABA receptor agonist activity; NCBI/PubChem records support analog/prodrug and GABA-A/GABA-B wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"High","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"High","rationale":"Mechanism is supported by direct receptor-binding pharmacology and NCBI/PubChem records.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"NCBI PubChem pharmacology records","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"NCBI PubChem pharmacology records; PubMed Lloyd 1982 GABA receptor pharmacology study","rationale":"PubChem supports the summary, and PubMed PMID 6121050 is a stronger primary pharmacology source for receptor agonist activity.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"NCBI/PubChem","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"NCBI/PubChem; PubMed","rationale":"The current tier is acceptable but incomplete if PMID 6121050 is added as a primary mechanism source.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"Limited data; hepatic metabolism and interaction concerns reported","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Limited data; hepatic-enzyme elevations and clinically relevant interaction concerns reported, including effects on phenytoin/carbamazepine metabolism and microsomal epoxide hydrolase inhibition.","rationale":"Peer-reviewed sources report elevated hepatic enzymes, symptomatic hepatic enzyme elevation in one case, phenytoin interaction, carbamazepine-metabolism effects, and microsomal epoxide hydrolase inhibition.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3098923/","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1029073/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3191894/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8222491/"]},{"current_value":"Liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver","rationale":"The hepatic-enzyme and hepatic-metabolism/interactions literature supports liver/hepatic handling as the relevant metabolism/toxicity organ category.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3098923/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8222491/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"Limited data","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Limited data","rationale":"No current FDA label with a standardized half-life range was identified. Non-label secondary records report pharmacokinetic values, but the row's limited-data wording is appropriately conservative.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"Historical/unspecified epilepsy; Focal; Generalized","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Historical/unspecified epilepsy; Focal; Generalized","rationale":"RCT evidence includes partial/complex partial epilepsy and severe epilepsies including generalized and partial subgroups.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6357772/","https: