nih.gov/6383790/"},{"label":"Loiseau1983","pmid":"6357772","proposed_action":"Keep","rationale":"PMID 6357772 is Loiseau et al., 'Double-blind crossover trial of progabide versus placebo in severe epilepsies.' The NCBI Bookshelf evidence review links the same PubMed record and identifies the crossover design. It supports placebo-controlled trial inclusion but not extractable differential RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom values from accessible evidence.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6357772/"},{"label":"Dam1983","pmid":"6403342","proposed_action":"Keep","rationale":"PMID 6403342 is progabide in partial complex seizures, explicitly randomized, double-blind, crossover, and placebo-controlled in the PubMed abstract/publication types. It supports placebo-controlled RCT inclusion but not extractable differential RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom values.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed search on 05-20-2026: no current label found for terms [progabide; Gabrene].","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA label API search on 05-20-2026: no current FDA label found for terms [progabide; Gabrene; Gabren; SL 76002].","reason":"DailyMed is not an allowed source for boxed-warning verification; FDA/openFDA is allowed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=progabide&limit=1","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=Gabrene&limit=1"]},{"current_value":"NCBI PubChem pharmacology records; FDA/DailyMed labeling; ANSM French medicines directory","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"NCBI/PubMed and NCBI PubChem pharmacology records; FDA/openFDA labeling; PubMed placebo-controlled trial reports; ANSM French medicines directory for French authorization facts only if an allowed source URL is retained.","reason":"Correct FDA source wording and add PubMed RCT/outcome support. French authorization facts still need a specific acceptable source decision.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6357772/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/"]},{"current_value":"NCBI PubChem pharmacology records","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"NCBI PubChem pharmacology records; PubMed Lloyd 1982 GABA receptor pharmacology study","reason":"Primary PubMed pharmacology evidence better supports the mechanism cell.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]}],"summary":"Progabide row is mostly directionally correct for mechanism, non-US/no-current-FDA-label status, epilepsy types, and RCT outcome non-extractability. Updates are needed for FDA boxed-warning source wording, missing aliases/search aliases, evidence-source wording, and overly absolute adverse-event availability wording. Exact French ANSM authorization/revocation dates remain missing-source under the audit's allowed-domain list."}
